      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Like the OP, I used to have this problem a couple of years back but at some point an update fixed it. Before, there was a 50/50 chance of this happening, but for the last 6 months this has gone up to a 90% chance.\n\nOn disconnect either through a crash or battery change, VRC will do one of two things:\n\n- Completely forget all audio devices, including microphone. Audio devices in Windows works as intended.\n\n- Lose audio from everyone who were in the instance when the crash happened. If a new person joins, their audio works fine. Rejoining the world solves this problem.\n\nSteamVR works as intended in all instances. On restart of VRC, audio devices come back.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-21T22:03:06.476Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is only happening in VRChat, so it is likely a VRC bug. I have a gen1 Vive headset with the wireless audio strap. Sometimes the headset disconnects through lag or my own body getting in the way of the receiver, or when I need to change batteries. Other games come back without issue when the headset powers back on and reconnects to my PC, but with VRC, the headset audio seems to bug. Sometimes I will come back to just world audio and nothing else, sometimes voice audio is missing but nothing else is, sometimes all audio is missing. The only thing that resolves the issue is restarting the game.",
